Why: Saved MDA sequence outputs were only inspectable as files, making it awkward to review RGB frames, depth images, and per-frame geometry or to loop through frames in a browser. The user wanted a simple result-checking demo inspired by Gradio/Rerun style viewers in vggt-omega and VGGT4D.

How: Added src/testing/result_viewer.py, a FastAPI browser viewer for run_inference_video.py outputs. It serves RGB images, colored depth images, frame stats, and WebGL point clouds reconstructed from raw/*.npz depth/rgb payloads with depth-edge filtering, point limits, playback controls, and per-frame looping. Added just viewer/viewer-bg/viewer-status/viewer-stop recipes and README usage notes. Verified with compileall, API curls, image endpoints, point-cloud payload generation, and a headless Chromium screenshot.
